# The shading options, as one picture.
#
# Both halves are the CURRENT build with different options, not two versions,
# because these four options all exist today and the question a player has is
# what turning them on does. For a release card use `before_tag=` instead, so
# the before half is the version that actually shipped.
#
# Build:  bash mods/voxel_characters/tools/render/card.sh \
#           mods/voxel_characters/tools/render/cards/shading.card shading.png

title=Voxel Characters: shading that suggests volume
sprite=red
frame=0
rung=35
yaw=0
cell=320

before_label=BEFORE
before_sub=flat slab, every shading option off
before_opt=front_shape:off,top_dome:off,ground_shade:off,top_edge:off

after_label=AFTER
after_sub=FRONT SHAPE MED, TOP DOME LOW, GROUND SHADE, TOP EDGE
after_opt=front_shape:0.17,top_dome:0.15,ground_shade:on,top_edge:on

point=0.50,0.10|TOP DOME|The top face steps into pixel aligned tones toward each run's edge, so the cap reads as domed instead of flat. No vertex moves, so the silhouette is untouched.
point=0.26,0.52|FRONT SHAPE|The front face is stepped into three tones toward the edge of each horizontal run. False roundness with no gradient and no new geometry.
point=0.74,0.22|TOP EDGE|Exposed top faces are darkened, which removes the bright cap that used to appear above a dark outline.
point=0.50,0.95|GROUND SHADE|The host's own contact shade on the lowest six pixels, so the body sits on the floor instead of hovering over it.
